// [imported] origin "data/standards/chemistry/Gly-formation.dat" (Choupo-2608 release) -- owned + sha256-verified by constant/propertyManifest
/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Gly-formation.dat -- a dissociation of glycine, written from the master:
      HGly  <=>  Gly + H+
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 2.351, dH1 = 4.00 kJ/mol, dCp -139 J/mol/K (grade AAA)
      pK2 = 9.780, dH2 = 44.2 kJ/mol, dCp -57 J/mol/K (grade AAB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is HGly, the form a case declares; this record carries step 2 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  The pK and dH are the evaluated values of Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen (7.31); the formation data are Miller & Smith-Magowan's (Table 3, with their Table 6 step enthalpies and entropies), which agree on the steps to 0.01 and 0.1 kJ/mol.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Gly; masters ( { ion HGly; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -9.78; dH 44200; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 359, and Section 7.31, p. 281: pK2 9.780, dH2 44.2 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
